# Build artifacts
/target
# ckdev-mutate proof, replay and broad-audit reports live under target/mutations/.
/target/mutations/
**/*.rs.bk
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED, deliberately — this workspace produces binaries
# (ck-plexus, ck-plexus-admin), not a library.
#
# Without it, two builds at the same source commit can link different
# dependency versions, and every deploy check we have — inode identity, build
# commit, discriminator strings — establishes SOURCE identity only. Measured on
# 2026-08-07: a single fresh resolve moved 11 packages, including rustls and
# http, which are on the path that carries vendor credentials. Those moves
# produce no git diff, so "same commit, different behaviour" would be
# unanswerable exactly when someone is asking it during an incident.
#
# It also makes CI mean something: without a committed lock, CI resolves fresh
# on every run and can attest a dependency set nobody ever built against.
node_modules/
dist/

# CortexKit layout: .cortexkit/ holds local tool state and internal documents,
# which are never committed. Only these shared, publishable paths are tracked.
# scripts/check-cortexkit-layout.sh enforces this.
/.cortexkit/*
!/.cortexkit/release-notes/
!/.cortexkit/skills/
!/.cortexkit/rules/
!/.cortexkit/WORKER.md

# OS
.DS_Store

# cortexkit-store lease files (runtime artifacts from tests)
*.lease

# Python bytecode from the script tests.
__pycache__/
